      {
        "title": "Are you learning Chinese?",
        "note": "**The many words for \"Chinese language\":**\n- **中文 Zhōngwén** — most common everyday term, safe default anywhere 🟢\n- **汉语 Hànyǔ** — formal/academic (HSK = 汉语水平考试) 🔵\n- **普通话 Pǔtōnghuà** — specifically standard Mandarin, mainland China 🌏\n- **国语 Guóyǔ** — same as 普通话 but used in Taiwan 🌏\n- **华语 Huáyǔ** — used in Southeast Asia (Singapore, Malaysia) 🌏\n- **中国话 Zhōngguóhuà** — colloquial, informal 🟡\n**说 shuō vs 讲 jiǎng:** Both mean \"to speak.\" 讲 is widely used in southern China, Taiwan, and overseas communities. Both are correct.\n**\"Do you speak Chinese?\" — base structure:**\n你会 **说/讲** + **中文/汉语/普通话/国语/华语** + 吗？\nMost common: 你会说中文吗 and 你会讲中文吗.",
